# An ESP32-S3 (four 32-bit slots on one line) greys the layouts it cannot carry and says why: a tap on a greyed one
# changes nothing and the card gives its reason, a layout it carries with a limit is taken at Apply. Preview
# only: no board on the bench has these capabilities, so a run with --board refuses it at the profile.
board s3-spi-320x240
display 1024 600
scene lyrics

tap "Preferences"
expect shown "Speaker layout"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.0

tap "Change" in "Speaker layout"
expect text "This board carries up to 4 speakers"
tap "5.1"
expect text "5.1 needs 6 slots"
expect text "16-bit slots would carry 8"
tap "Apply"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.0

tap "2.1"
expect text "Works, with a limit"
tap "Apply"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.1

tap "Change" in "Speaker layout"
tap "Build yours"
tap "9"
expect text "Nine around you needs 9 slots"
tap "Cancel"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.1

tap "Change" in "Speaker layout"
tap "2.0"
tap "Apply"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.0
